//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// H Ticks — FVG / iFVG : 15m bias -> ANY ONE context timeframe (1m / 2m / 3m / 5m) inverts -> retest of THAT gap ->
//                         decisive 30s inversion linked to THAT context -> entry at close -> structural stop -> fixed 1R
//
// REQUIRES A STANDARD 30-SECOND CHART. Anything else shows "Switch to a standard 30-second chart" and generates nothing.
// CONTEXT TIMEFRAMES: Auto = 1m, 2m, 3m and 5m each keep their OWN independent state (inversion, retest, leg extreme).
//   ANY ONE of them can supply a valid setup; no agreement between them is required; no timeframe waits for a larger one.
//   A newer context replaces only the pending context of the SAME timeframe. Retests are never matched across timeframes.
// SEQUENCE per context (all mechanical, all on confirmed candles; no score, no win-rate claim):
//   1. 15m BIAS: confirmed 15m pivots (2 left / 2 right, strict), available only after the second right-side candle completes;
//      a confirmed 15m CLOSE strictly beyond the latest unbroken swing (available before the breaking candle began) sets it.
//      UNKNOWN until the first break. Required at context creation and at entry.
//   2. CONTEXT: a source FVG inverts on a confirmed source CLOSE strictly beyond its far boundary (wick / equality is not
//      enough), in the bias direction, inside an enabled entry window. Cancelled by a later close of its OWN timeframe back
//      through the zone, by a 15m bias reversal, or at the end of its entry window.
//   3. RETEST: a later 30s candle (opening at/after the inversion confirmation) intersects that context gap. Zone is kept.
//   4. TRIGGER: a fresh 30s FVG (formation candle opens at/after the confirmation, overlaps the context gap) inverts in the
//      setup direction on a candle strictly after the retest candle, and that inversion candle is DECISIVE (Standard/Strong).
//   5. STOP = beyond the retest-leg extreme of THAT context (first retest candle .. entry candle) +/- max(1 tick, 0.10 x
//      previous 30s ATR); ENTRY = the inversion candle's confirmed close; TARGET = exactly the same tick distance (1R).
//   6. CLEAR PATH: no opposing 15m/1H/4H gap on [entry, target] and the target ends >= 1 tick before the nearest unconsumed
//      3m swing level. Missing coverage is UNKNOWN, never clear.
//   SELECTION: every pending context is evaluated independently through ALL gates on every trigger bar. Failing candidates
//   never block passing ones. If several pass, 5m > 3m > 2m > 1m decides (a tie-break only). Exactly one entry is created;
//   all pending contexts are then discarded. Gates: same window instance, < 3 entries per instance, one unresolved setup.
// Timing: all state changes and drawings happen on confirmed 30s bars. Alerts only on confirmed realtime bars.
// Verification: see H_Ticks_FVG_iFVG_NOTES.md (code review + Python model only; NOT compiled in TradingView, NOT Bar-Replay tested).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INDICATOR (not a strategy). Outcomes: OPEN / TARGET_HIT / STOP_HIT / AMBIGUOUS on 30s candles strictly AFTER the entry
// candle (opening price first, then the range). No slippage, costs or time exit; an estimate, not broker results.
indicator("H Ticks — FVG / iFVG", shorttitle = "H Ticks", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 500)

const string GRP_CTX = "Context timeframe"
const string GRP_WIN = "Entry windows (Asia 09:00 Tokyo -> 08:00 London, NY 09:45-11:30, NY 14:30-15:30; DST-aware; Mon-Fri)"
const string GRP_Q   = "Setup quality"
const string GRP_APP = "Chart appearance"
const string GRP_ST  = "Statistics"
const string GRP_DBG = "Debug"
const string GRP_AL  = "Alerts"
string inCtxSel = input.string("Auto (1m, 2m, 3m, 5m)", "Context timeframe", options = ["Auto (1m, 2m, 3m, 5m)", "1m only", "2m only", "3m only", "5m only"], group = GRP_CTX, tooltip = "Auto: each of 1m, 2m, 3m and 5m is tracked independently and ANY ONE can supply a valid setup (no agreement required). If several pass on the same 30s trigger, 5m > 3m > 2m > 1m picks the one entry (tie-break only).")
bool   inWinAsia = input.bool(true, "Window A: Asia open -> London open", group = GRP_WIN)
bool   inWinAm = input.bool(true, "Window B: New York morning 09:45-11:30", group = GRP_WIN, tooltip = "Start inclusive, end exclusive. BOTH the context inversion and the entry must belong to the same window instance (max 3 entries per instance, one unresolved setup at a time).")
bool   inWinPm = input.bool(true, "Window C: New York afternoon 14:30-15:30", group = GRP_WIN)
string inPreset = input.string("Standard", "Impulse preset (decisive 30s inversion candle)", options = ["Standard", "Strong"], group = GRP_Q, tooltip = "Standard: body >= 0.8 x prev ATR, body/range >= 0.65, close in the outer 20% of the range. Strong: 1.0 x, 0.70, outer 15%. Both: body points in the setup direction and the close extends beyond the trigger gap boundary by max(1 tick, 0.10 x prev ATR). Starting parameters, not optimised or proven.")
int    inMinTick = input.int(1, "Minimum gap size (ticks, all gap sources)", minval = 1, group = GRP_Q, tooltip = "Gaps at least this wide are detected and may form contexts, triggers and obstacles.")
bool   inShowPair = input.bool(true, "Show the context gap + 30s trigger gap of every setup", group = GRP_APP)
bool   inShowHtf = input.bool(true, "Show nearby HTF gaps", group = GRP_APP, tooltip = "Display only. Obstacle checks always use ALL tracked 15m/1H/4H gaps, hidden or not.")
bool   inShowRR = input.bool(true, "Show risk/reward shading", group = GRP_APP)
string inTheme = input.string("Light", "Theme (labels and tables)", options = ["Light", "Dark"], group = GRP_APP, tooltip = "Light: black entry line. Dark: white entry line (black would be invisible). Tables always use opaque backgrounds.")
bool   inStats = input.bool(true, "Show the five-day results table", group = GRP_ST)
bool   inStatus = input.bool(true, "Show compact status", group = GRP_ST)
bool   inDebug = input.bool(false, "Show the per-context funnel and label rejected triggers", group = GRP_DBG, tooltip = "Funnel: inversions, admitted contexts, retests, eligible 30s inversions, impulse / stop-risk / clear-path passes, entries; block counters list the FIRST failed gate of each candidate (counted once).")
bool   alEntry = input.bool(true, "Alert on each new entry", group = GRP_AL)
bool   alTarget = input.bool(true, "Alert when a setup hits its target", group = GRP_AL)
bool   alStop = input.bool(true, "Alert when a setup hits its stop", group = GRP_AL)

